  "body": "Turns **Configure Claude Code** from a two-key connect screen into a real settings editor, on top of the API from #115. The existing \"Choose how you connect\" section is unchanged above it.\n\n## What it looks like\n\nRendered from the generated catalog, so the controls track upstream: **504 editable settings**, each drawn as what it actually is — a dropdown with the documented options for an enum, a number field for a number, a masked field for a credential, a JSON textarea for an array or object.\n\nVolume is handled with **search + a curated default**, not accordions:\n\n| | |\n| --- | --- |\n| Default view | **101 settings** people actually reach for |\n| `Show all` | the remaining 400 |\n| Search | always covers **everything**, including entries the view filters would hide — typing a variable name in full always finds it |\n| `Configured only` | narrows to what the file sets |\n\nEdits collect as pending changes and are written only from a **review dialog** showing a real diff — key, before, after — plus any warning the backend attached, and a note that the file is backed up first.\n\n## Two bugs the browser found that the API tests could not\n\n- **`permissions.defaultMode` rendered as a text box, not a dropdown.** The enum table is keyed by the name the docs use in their own table (`defaultMode`) while nested entries are catalogued with their parent prefix (`permissions.defaultMode`), so the lookup missed and **every nested enum silently degraded to free text**. The API test *\"every enum entry has values\"* still passed — because the entries were no longer enums. Lookup now tries the full key then the bare leaf.\n- **A value the editor had just written read back as unset.** `read_values` returned the `permissions` object but not the dotted leaf the UI addresses, so writing `permissions.defaultMode` and reloading showed \"Not set\". Nested groups are now flattened to dotted leaves, parent included, with 4 regression tests.\n\n## And a visual bug this page already had\n\nThe 5.7.2 redesign used `var(--space-N)` tokens that were **never defined**, so every rule using them was invalid and dropped — the connect cards shipped with **no padding and no gap**. Defining the scale fixes them (measured 0px → 16px).\n\n## The three traps, surfaced not just handled\n\n- A presence-read variable carries a **`presence` badge**, and turning it off shows in the diff as *\"1 → removed\"* with a line explaining that writing `0` would have left it enabled.\n- A masked secret is **never echoed back as a write**: the field starts empty with a *\"Set — type to replace\"* placeholder, so applying without touching it can't overwrite the real key with asterisks.\n- A **managed policy** that outranks the file is called out above the list, naming the file and the keys it pins.\n\n## Verification\n\nReal browser, live server, throwaway home on port 8173 (**WSL :8082 never touched**, still answering 200):\n\n- 101 rows default / 504 with Show all; sections grouped, Permissions first.\n- Toggled `DISABLE_TELEMETRY` off, set `permissions.defaultMode`, set `API_TIMEOUT_MS`. The diff showed `1 → removed` with the presence explanation plus two `(not set) →` rows. **On disk afterwards**: key removed, timeout written as a string, defaultMode set, credential untouched, `.fcc-backup` holding the original.\n- Reloaded — all three read back under the keys the UI addresses.\n- Searched `VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_5_OPUS` (outside the default view) and found it; `Configured only` listed exactly the five keys set.\n- **No console errors.** Checked in all four themes — name, description and badge colours all resolve from semantic tokens, nothing hardcoded.\n- Full suite **3779 passed**, same 14 environment-baseline failures as an untouched worktree.\n\nMINOR bump **5.8.0 → 5.9.0**.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TWCKNkSxNEfus8GfcqXnQD\n",
