    "message": "feat(admin): guided settings editor on the Configure Claude Code page\n\nThe page could write two keys. Everything else about Claude Code -- model,\neffort, permissions, tool limits, telemetry, terminal behaviour -- meant hand\nediting ~/.claude/settings.json. This adds the editor on top of the API from\n#115, and keeps the existing \"Choose how you connect\" section unchanged above it.\n\nRendered from the generated catalog, so the controls track upstream: 504\neditable settings, each drawn as what it actually is. A dropdown with the\ndocumented options for an enum, a number field for a number, a masked field for\na credential, a JSON textarea for an array or object.\n\nVolume is handled with search and a curated default rather than accordions,\nwhich is the shape this dashboard already wants. The default view is 101\nsettings people actually reach for; \"Show all\" reveals the remaining 400; search\nalways covers everything, including entries the view filters would hide, so\ntyping a variable name in full always finds it. \"Configured only\" narrows to\nwhat the file sets.\n\nEdits collect as pending changes and are written only from a review dialog that\nshows a real diff -- key, before, after -- plus any warning the backend\nattached, and a note that the file is backed up first. Nothing is written until\nApply.\n\nTwo bugs found by driving the page in a real browser, neither visible to the\nAPI tests:\n\n- permissions.defaultMode rendered as a free-text box instead of a dropdown.\n  The enum table is keyed by the name the docs use in their own table\n  (defaultMode) while nested entries are catalogued with their parent prefix\n  (permissions.defaultMode), so the lookup missed and every nested enum\n  silently degraded to text. The API test \"every enum entry has values\" still\n  passed, because the entries were no longer enums. The lookup now tries the\n  full key then the bare leaf.\n- A value the editor had just written read back as unset. read_values returned\n  the permissions object but not the dotted leaf the UI addresses, so writing\n  permissions.defaultMode and reloading showed \"Not set\". Nested groups are now\n  flattened to dotted leaves, parent included, with tests.\n\nAlso fixed a shipped visual bug this page already had: the 5.7.2 redesign used\nvar(--space-N) tokens that were never defined, so every rule using them was\ninvalid and dropped -- the connect cards rendered with no padding and no gap.\nDefining the scale fixes them (measured 0px -> 16px).\n\nThe three value traps are surfaced, not just handled:\n- A presence-read variable carries a \"presence\" badge, and turning it off shows\n  in the diff as \"removed\" with a line explaining that writing 0 would have\n  left it enabled.\n- A masked secret is never echoed back as a write: the field starts empty with\n  a \"Set -- type to replace\" placeholder, so applying without touching it\n  cannot overwrite the real key with asterisks.\n- A managed policy that outranks the file is called out above the list, naming\n  the file and the keys it pins.\n\nVerification, in a real browser against a live server on a throwaway home\n(port 8173, WSL :8082 never touched and still answering 200):\n- 101 rows in the default view, 504 with Show all, sections grouped with\n  Permissions first.\n- Toggled DISABLE_TELEMETRY off, set permissions.defaultMode, set\n  API_TIMEOUT_MS: the diff showed \"1 -> removed\" with the presence explanation\n  and two \"(not set) ->\" rows; the file on disk afterwards had the key removed,\n  the timeout written as a string, defaultMode set, the credential untouched,\n  and a .fcc-backup holding the original.\n- Reloaded and confirmed all three read back under the keys the UI addresses.\n- Searched a variable outside the default view (VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_5_OPUS)\n  and found it; \"Configured only\" listed exactly the five keys set.\n- No console errors. Checked in all four themes: name, description and badge\n  colours all resolve from semantic tokens, so nothing is hardcoded.\n- 4 new tests for the nested round trip; full suite 3779 passed with the same\n  14 environment-baseline failures as an untouched worktree.\n\nMINOR bump 5.8.0 -> 5.9.0.",
